= Phuong Luu Vo
Associate Professor, School of Computer Science and Engineering, International University (VNU-HCM)

~~~
{}{img_left}{images/portrait.svg}{Portrait of Phuong Luu Vo}{175}{}{}
Welcome! I am an Associate Professor at the School of Computer Science and Engineering,
International University -- Vietnam National University Ho Chi Minh City, where I lead the
*Network Optimization and Distributed Learning* group.

My research covers distributed computing and distributed learning, machine learning and deep
reinforcement learning, and wireless and mobile networking with the Internet of Things. Recent
work is on semantic communication, federated and edge learning, and adaptive video streaming
over multipath and cache-enabled networks. Please have a look at my
[publications.html Publications] and at the work of my [students.html research group].

I am currently looking for motivated students for *prethesis*, *thesis*, and *internship*
projects. See [joining.html For Students] for what that involves and how to get in touch.
~~~

